# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Ozylix SPA — clean URL routing
#
# READ THIS BEFORE CHANGING HOSTS. GitHub Pages IGNORES this file: it
# serves a real file or a 404, so /shop and every /product/... URL in
# sitemap.xml returned HTTP 404 to Googlebot and could never be indexed.
# That is why Search Console showed zero impressions with a valid
# sitemap. Cloudflare Pages honours these rules and returns 200.
#
# 200 is a REWRITE, not a redirect: the URL stays as the customer and
# Googlebot see it, and index.html is served underneath. The app reads
# location.pathname on boot and shows the right page.
#
# Only routes the app can actually render from a cold URL belong here.
# Its boot list is _validPages in index.html:
#   home, shop, blog, about, contact, faq, advisor, product
# Rewriting a path the app cannot render would serve the home page under
# that URL — a soft 404, which is worse for search than an honest 404.
#
# Cloudflare limits: 2,000 static rules and 100 dynamic (splat) rules.
# One splat is used below, so there is room to spare.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ── Product pages ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# A splat, not sixteen lines. Every product URL in sitemap.xml was
# missing from this file, so the most commercially valuable pages on the
# site would still have 404'd after the move. The splat also covers
# products added later, which a hand-written list would not.
/product/*                  /index.html  200

# ── Page routes ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/shop                       /index.html  200
/blog                       /index.html  200
/about                      /index.html  200
/contact                    /index.html  200
/faq                        /index.html  200
/advisor                    /index.html  200

# ── Kept from the previous file ────────────────────────────────────
# These three are NOT in sitemap.xml and are NOT in _validPages, so the
# app shows the home page under them. Harmless for a shared link, but do
# not add them to the sitemap while that is true.
/b2b                        /index.html  200
/wishlist                   /index.html  200
/subscriptions              /index.html  200

# Deliberately absent: /cart, /checkout, /account, /thankyou. They are
# session state, not destinations — nothing should link to or index them,
# and the app cannot rebuild them from a cold URL anyway.
